 {:seon.task/name "the-agents-links-are-refs"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-23: \"keep the data in the database for easy pulling and rendering\"; a page is an entity and what one ref away (a-page-is-an-entity-and-its-neighbors needs this). What exists: the links between an agent, its run, its turns and its messages are names, not refs, so no pull follows them: :seon.attempt/agent is a keyword (:a3), :seon.turn/attempt and :seon.message/to are strings (the run's id), and :seon.agent/id :a3 is one identity for every boot's a3, so two boots' agents and their evaluations are one entity. Root (:seon.root/id) holds its agents only in its process's memory (its view), so its entity has no link to them; an agent's live state (pid, memory, the form running, its status) and the procs' numbers (the writer's batches, the fork server's forks) are not in the store at all. Correct: each link a ref (:db.type/ref): run -> agent, turn -> run, message -> run (and -> its sender), agent -> the root that started it; an agent entity per agent per boot (identity [boot id], the boot its root's :seon.root/boot); an agent's live state and each proc's numbers recorded as facts on its entity when they change, by their owner (root records an agent's status when its view changes; the writer its own numbers when it commits), never polled, no write on an idle system. No migration: the stored keys change with the run rename (jolt/rename-run), whose merge erases the store (DECISIONS). Deletes every string or keyword join between these entities (the d/q over :seon.turn/attempt, the message reader's lookup by :to, root's view as a second source of what an agent is)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.task-test/an-agents-links-pull-from-its-root seon.task-test/an-agents-live-state-is-facts-on-its-entity seon.procs-test/root-records-what-it-observes-of-its-agents}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-walk"
  :seon.task/plan "The one mechanism every view of Seon's data goes through: the owner's window, root's page and the model's context (owner, 2026-10-23: \"locations should be based on a starting EID and we pull from there to render the data what one hop away\"; \"I want logical solution for everything so we aren't inventing new shit\"; \"rendered with render functions not manual wiring\"). What v1 did (~/src/seon/resources/seon/schemas/seon.agent.edn :agent, render/walk.clj neighborhood at :seon.render/distance 1): an entity's schema declares the neighbours a view of it shows as :seon.render/units, attributes in pull's own syntax (a leading _ the reverse ref), components included; the walk pulls the entity and those attributes, and each neighbour renders by its own schema's render. Bring the rule, not v1's 1263 lines (most are SCI caps and caches). Build: (1) :seon.render/units on the schemas this needs: the agent's (:seon.agent/agent-fact: its run :seon.attempt/_agent, its evaluations :seon.cluster.eval/_agent, its root), the run's (:seon.attempt/attempt-fact: its task, its turns :seon.turn/_attempt, the messages to it :seon.message/_to), the task's (its plan, proofs), root's (:seon.root/root-fact: its agents :seon.agent/_root, the open problems); (2) seon.render/walk: one d/pull of an eid with its own attributes and its units (on a branch: the branch's db, or seon.union's U for what spans branches, ids issued once store-wide, docs/storage.md#ids), plus what its string attributes cite (seon.ref/parse, each citation pulled at the depth its delimiter asks, as seon.context pulls it), answering the tree as data; (3) the tree printed by the one printer (seon.print with seon.render/nested): the root of the walk by its render :as :block, each unit :as :tile, both faces in one walk (:ai text, :html hiccup), and beside the result which render made which part from which entity and attribute (provenance, data). What is not useful is cut at its producer or given a focused render on its schema, never filtered by a view (owner: \"if shit isn't useful we either cut it at the producer or make specific renders to help focus the context or html\"). Read first: docs/render.md, seon.render (render-of, nested, print-ai), seon.print, seon.ref, seon.context's pulls (what it pulls today and at which depth), v1's walk. Replaces nothing yet: the-page-is-the-walk and the-context-is-evaluations delete the hand-built producers."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.render/the-agents-links-are-refs"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/a-walk-is-its-entity-and-its-units seon.render-test/a-walk-pulls-what-its-strings-cite seon.render-test/a-walk-names-the-render-of-each-part seon.render-cost-test/a-walk-reads-its-entity-and-one-hop}}
