  :seon.task/plan "Every page is the walk of one entity (seon.render/the-walk) through its :html face (owner, 2026-10-23: \"no separate run view it's part of the agents view\"; \"root is also an agents view, it just has different focus since it should be linked up with all the agents it's running on the system, the system health, etc\"). What exists: seon.render.proc/zoom-value assembles an agent's window by hand from root's view, main's run and the branch, joined by strings (turn-rows, eval-records, a tile list, a run-or-agent branch, a :turn-ctx cache), the /attempt/{id} route beside /agent/{id}, and root's page a second producer (seon.render.ui/system-page, agent-card and the grid). Build: a location is an entity (/agent/{id} resolves to the agent's eid in root's boot, / to root's); the page is the walk: the entity as the main pane (:block), its units the column (:tile) in their declared order, each a link that moves the eid; a unit is rendered again when a commit changes its entity (the render proc's events), never polled. The owner's window shows the same evaluations the model's context shows (seon.context/the-context-is-evaluations), through the :html face, with the chat input (evaluate, message, interrupt, release) as today. Deletes zoom-value, turn-rows, eval-records' joins, the /attempt route, system-page's hand-built sections, agent-card and the grid (one :tile render of an agent replaces both), the tile list and :turn-ctx. A browser subagent compares each page against the facts (notes/browser-tester.md)."
